abstract: >-
  Two separately run, machine-checkable audits of the mathematics, code, citations and quotations in
  Joel Dietz's "Why Michael Levin Is 77.6++% Right on Platonic Ingress" and Nathan Sweet's "Why Michael
  Levin's Bubble Sort 'Revelation' Is Misunderstood", including runs of the original threaded code of
  Zhang, Goldstein & Levin (2025), exact combinatorics, Lean 4 proofs, DOI resolution and a cross-audit
  article. The audits were performed with AI coding agents (Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Cowork; OpenAI
  Codex with GPT-6.1 Sol), which are tools, not authors.
